## Round 3: judge r1 result and the arms color try 2

### Judge result of round 1

The judge result file
`measure/runs/asset_storytime_l2_family_words_20261107/judge-fw-r1-color.json` holds 18 files with
18 pass and 0 fail on color try 1. The maker did not rate any picture.

### The arms row and the orchestrator decision

The arms row passed the first judge. The second judge on the arms file alone,
`measure/runs/asset_storytime_l2_family_words_20261107/judge-fw-r1-color-arms-second.json`, also
passed it. Both judges record the same note: the pointing finger touches Nan's chest near the
star, and it does not reach the raised arm.

Orchestrator decision 2026-11-07: the PM rule says a body-part picture shows a child pointing to
the part. The arms try 1 picture does not show that, so try 1 counts as a failed try under the PM
rule. The arms row gets color try 2. The other 17 rows pass on try 1 and get no new call.

### The change of the arms spec

Only the picture sentences of the arms `colorPrompt` changed. The new sentences hold one arm
straight out to the side at shoulder height, and they put the index finger of the other hand on
that arm. Every other sentence of the prompt stays as it was, and every other field of the file
stays as it was. The `goal` changed because the pose changed. It now reads "One picture of Nan
that shows the word arms: she holds one arm out to the side, and a finger of her other hand
touches that arm." The `mustShow` list stays as it was.

The spec test command
`HEAVY_MIN_AVAIL_MB=1500 bash /home/daniebo/Desktop/advantage-pr/scripts/jobs/heavy-run.sh -c './node_modules/.bin/vitest run tests/storytime-family-word-specs.test.ts --maxWorkers=1'`
